<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">Met Based Drugs</journal-id><journal-title>Metal-Based Drugs</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0793-0291</issn><publisher><publisher-name>Hindawi Publishing Corporation</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">18472909</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2366831</article-id>        <article-id pub-id-type="pii">S0793029199000270</article-id>        <article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1155/MBD.1999.177</article-id>    <article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Research Article</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Hormone Anchored Metal Complexes. 1. Synthesis, Structure,Spectroscopy and <italic>In Vitro</italic> Antitumor Activity of TestosteroneAcetate Thiosemicarbazone and its Metal Complexes</article-title></title-group><contrib-group>        <contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Murugkar</surname><given-names>Anupa</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff1">1</xref></contrib>        <contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Unnikrishnan</surname><given-names>Bindu </given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff1">1</xref></contrib>        <contrib contrib-type="author" corresp="yes"><name><surname>Padhye</surname><given-names>Subhash</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff1">1</xref></contrib>        <contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Bhonde</surname><given-names>Ramesh</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff2">2</xref></contrib>        <contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Teat</surname><given-names>Simon</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff3">3</xref></contrib>        <contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Triantafillou</surname><given-names>Evangelia</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff4">4</xref></contrib>        <contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Sinn</surname><given-names>Ekkehard</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff4">4</xref></contrib>                </contrib-group>                     <aff id="aff1"><label>1</label>                <addr-line>Department of Chemistry</addr-line>                <addr-line>University of Pune</addr-line>                <addr-line>Pune</addr-line>                <addr-line>411007</addr-line>                <country>India</country>            </aff>            <aff id="aff2"><label>2</label>                <addr-line>National Centre for Cell Science</addr-line>                <addr-line>Ganeshkhind</addr-line>                <addr-line>Pune</addr-line>                <addr-line>411007</addr-line>                <country>India</country>            </aff>            <aff id="aff3"><label>3</label>                <addr-line>CLRC Daresbury</addr-line>                <addr-line>Cheshire</addr-line>                <addr-line>WA4 4AD</addr-line>                <country>UK</country>            </aff>            <aff id="aff4"><label>4</label>             <addr-line>Department of Chemistry</addr-line>                <addr-line>University of Hull</addr-line>                <addr-line>Hull</addr-line>                <addr-line>HU6 7RX</addr-line>                <country>UK</country>            </aff>                  <pub-date pub-type="ppub"><year>1999</year></pub-date><volume>6</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>177</fpage><lpage>182</lpage><history><date date-type="received"><day>31</day><month>3</month><year>1999</year></date><date date-type="accepted"><day>30</day><month>4</month><year>1999</year></date></history><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; 1999 Hindawi Publishing Corporation.</copyright-statement><copyright-year>1999</copyright-year><copyright-holder>Hindawi Publishing Corporation</copyright-holder><license license-type="open-access" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/"><p>This is an open access article distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.</p></license></permissions><abstract>        <p>Testosterone acetate thiosemicarbazone (TATSC, 17-&#x003b2;-hydroxyandrost-4-one acetate thiosemicarbazone)was synthesized and characterized by single crystal X-ray structure determination. The copper and platinumcomplexes of this steroid derivative were synthesized and characterized by spectroscopy and electrochemiatry.The in vitro activity of these compounds against human breast cancer cell line MCF-7 was tested. Thehighest activity was found for the [Pt(TATSC)Cl<sub>1</sub>] followed by [Cu(TATSC)Cl<sub>2</sub>] and the ligand incompariosn with cisplatin.</p>    </abstract></article-meta></front></article>